{
	"ID": "io.gravwell.llm_observability",
	"Name": "LLM Observability",
	"Desc": "Turn the traffic flowing through the Gravwell LLM proxy into something you can chart and hunt through: token spend and latency per model, what the models are calling tools for, and meaning-based hunts over the prompts themselves.",
	"Readme": "This kit makes the traffic captured by the Gravwell LLM proxy useful. It ships dashboards for token spend, latency, tool use, and upstream errors, plus a library of *semantic* hunts that search prompts by meaning rather than by keyword.\n\nThe LLM Observability kit is licensed under the BSD 2-Clause license and the contents are available on [Github](https://github.com/gravwell/kits/tree/main/llm_observability).\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Gravwell 5.10 or later.\n- The **Gravwell LLM ingester** deployed as a proxy in front of your model provider. See the *Deploying the LLM Proxy* playbook.\n- For the semantic hunts only: the **vector preprocessor** attached to an LLM listener, and `Embedding-URL` / `Embedding-Model` in the webserver's `[AI]` section. See the *Enabling Semantic Search* playbook. Everything else in the kit works without them.\n- For the `llm-triage` agent only: an LLM configured on the deployment.\n\nSet the `LLM_TAG` configuration macro to whatever `Tag-Name` your listener writes to.\n\n## Changelog\n**1.0: Initial Release**\n- dashboard (5)\n- file (2)\n- license (1)\n- macro (8)\n- playbook (4)\n- resource (2)\n  - example ingester config (1)\n  - AI agent (1)\n- searchlibrary (25)\n  - observability queries (18)\n  - semantic hunts (7)\n- template (2)\n",
